  "the_difference_explained_numerically": "130 routes, 964 dispatches, 38 kernels are three different things and the ratios say what each is. A route lowers to 7.42 dispatches on average, because one mixer route becomes a norm, an input projection, a rope or conv stage, the attention or recurrence itself, and an output projection. A kernel is dispatched 25.4 times per token, because the same program runs once per layer. Counting dispatches as routes would overstate the semantic width of the program 7.4x; counting kernels as routes would understate it 3.4x.",
